  "rationale": "Blocking h3_2:reach and h1_0:reach makes crown:obtain unreachable. Blocking h3_2:reach cuts h4_2:reach (an AND step) and removes the h3_2 route into h4_3:reach. Blocking h1_0:reach disables the AND steps h2_0:escalate and h2_1:reach. With those gone, h3_3:reach is cut, which kills h4_1:obtain, and h3_1:access is cut, which removes the other route into h4_3:reach. One block is not enough. If only h3_2:reach is blocked, the path h1_0 -> h2_0 -> h3_3 -> h4_1 -> crown stays open. If only h1_0:reach is blocked, h1_1:pivot still reaches h3_2:reach, then h4_3:reach, then crown. No other single step lies on every path to the target."
